# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same two variables in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Leave BOTH blank to run TaxHelper in local-only mode: no accounts, no network,
# everything stays in the browser. The app is fully functional that way.
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC. They ship inside the JavaScript bundle and are
# meant to be readable by anyone. Your data is protected by Row Level Security
# (supabase/schema.sql), not by hiding these.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here, or in any VITE_* variable. It bypasses
# row-level security completely and would expose every user's data.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The deployed https URL, used as the target for password-reset and email
# confirmation links. REQUIRED for the desktop build: there the page is served
# from app://taxhelper, which Supabase will not accept as a redirect, so it
# falls back to the project Site URL (localhost by default) and the link dies.
# Must also be listed under Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration.
VITE_SITE_URL=
